% =============================================================================
% rill sequent rules — the ○ next-time modality (TODO_0203, THY_0042)
% =============================================================================
%
% rill's backward judgment = [ill.rules, fill.rules] (inherited BY REFERENCE —
% calculus.load takes a rules-file list; ILL's fragment + the four μ/ν unfold
% rules) plus the ○ rule below. .rules files have no @extends, so the list
% [ill.rules, fill.rules, rill.rules] is assembled in rill's loader.
% =============================================================================

@formulas A, B, C

% Next-time introduction (○R). To promise A at the NEXT tick, prove A now using
% only resources that PERSIST across the tick: the linear context must be empty.
% A linear resource consumed now cannot be re-offered next tick — only persistent
% (!) resources, or the tail of a signal, advance. Promotion-shaped
% (G ; |- ○A <- G ; |- A): the empty-linear conclusion plus one premise sets
% requiresEmptyDelta, so ○R fires ONLY when the linear pool is empty — exactly
% the temporal no-carry-forward discipline. Positive ⇒ non-invertible (focus).
%
% This is the single ○ rule. There is NO ○-left rule: an ○A is never usable in
% the present (that is what makes ○ a genuine modality — non-collapse). Guarded
% signals νX.(A & ○X) coinduct via the ν back-edge (GTC progress = the νR unfold);
% ○R advances the persistent context across each tick to reach the companion.
next_r: G ; |- O A
  <- G ; |- A
  @pretty "○R"
  @invertible false.
